# P4 REVISION v3.x (M5_CHIP=v3). Added on top of sdkconfig.defaults by the
# root CMakeLists.txt. To build:
#     idf.py -B build_v3 -DM5_CHIP=v3 build
# (or ./flash.sh, which reads the device's revision and picks on its own).
#
# The IDF warns in its own Kconfig: v3.0 onward and v1.x have "huge hardware
# difference" - a binary for one does NOT run on the other (the bootloader
# rejects the revision). Nothing in the system's code depends on the
# revision beyond the max clock (400 MHz here, 360 on v1 - read from
# CONFIG_ESP_DEFAULT_CPU_FREQ_MHZ, see TAB5_CPU_MAX_MHZ in hal/tab5_power.hpp).
#
# THIS PROFILE BUILDS, BUT HAS NOT BEEN TESTED ON HARDWARE: we don't have a P4 v3.
# CONFIG_ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3 is not set
CONFIG_ESP32P4_REV_MIN_300=y
CONFIG_ESP_DEFAULT_CPU_FREQ_MHZ_400=y
